Package: vellum
Version: @VERSION@
Section: editors
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Maintainer: Matthew Hagrelius <matthew@hagreli.us>
Homepage: https://github.com/mhagrelius/vellum
Description: Markdown reader and editor for the GNOME desktop
 Vellum shows a Markdown document as it would be published, while it is
 still the file you are editing. The syntax characters are hidden until the
 cursor reaches them, so the document reads as prose and stays editable.
 .
 Eight reading styles — Adwaita, Newsprint, Academic, Sepia, Book, Terminal,
 Contrast and Typewriter — each set the whole page: face, measure, leading,
 heading treatment, rules and colour, in light and dark.
